  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In ammonium<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>phosphomolybdate, the oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mo</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Phosphomolybdate is an anion containing both phosphorus and molybdenum, with the chemical formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>12</mn><msub><mi>MoO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>The ammonium ion has a total charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and the phosphate ion has a total charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Therefore, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>MoO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> units in the compound must have a total charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><p>Each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MoO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> unit contains one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mo</mi></math> atom and three <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> atoms. The total oxidation state of the three <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;atoms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, since each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> atom has an oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mo</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>Mo</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
